<h3><a name="text" id="text">Text</a></h3>
	<blockquote>
	<h3>Choice 1: Change seconders to 2Q [3:1]</h3>
	<p>General Resolutions are an important framework within the Debian Project. Yet, in a project the size of Debian, the current requirements to initiate one are too small.
	<p>Therefore the Debian project resolves that
	<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
	<li> The constitution gets changed to not require K developers to sponsor a resolution, but floor(2Q). [see &sect;4.2(1)]</li>
	<li> Delaying a decision of a Delegate or the DPL [&sect;4.2(2.2)], as well as resolutions against a shortening of discussion/voting period or to overwrite a TC decision [&sect;4.2(2.3)] requires floor(Q) developers to sponsor the resolution.</li>
	<li> the definition of K gets erased from the constitution. [&sect;4.2(7)]</li>
	</ol>
	<p> (Numbers in brackets are references to sections in the constitution).
	</blockquote>
	<hr>
<h3><a name="amendmentproposera" id="amendmentproposera">Amendment Proposer A</a></h3>
	<p>Joerg Jaspert [<a href="mailto:joerg@debian.org">joerg@debian.org</a>] [<a href='https://lists.debian.org/debian-vote/2009/03/msg00094.html'>text of proposal</a>]
	</p>
<h3><a name="amendmentsecondsa" id="amendmentsecondsa">Amendment Seconds A</a></h3>
      <ol>
